{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 34, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a movie that tells the story of the founding of facebook and the subsequent lawsuits that followed. the film is directed by david fincher and written by aaron sorkin, who is known for his fast-paced and witty dialogue. the movie stars jesse eisenberg as mark zuckerberg, the co-founder and ceo of facebook, and andrew garfield as eduardo saverin, zuckerberg's friend and business partner.\n\nthe movie begins with mark zuckerberg, a sophomore at harvard university, who is trying to get over a recent break-up with his girlfriend. zuckerberg is a brilliant computer programmer and creates a website called facemash, which allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive. the website becomes a huge success, but also generates a lot of controversy and gets zuckerberg into trouble with the university administration.\n\nlater, zuckerberg is approached by cameron and tyler winklevoss, two twin brothers who are also students at harvard, to create a social networking site exclusively for harvard students. zuckerberg agrees to work on the project, but eventually drops out and creates his own social networking site, which he calls thefacebook. the site quickly gains popularity and zuckerberg becomes an overnight sensation.\n\nhowever, the success of thefacebook also leads to a lot of problems for zuckerberg. eduardo saverin, who is zuckerberg's friend and business partner, becomes increasingly frustrated with zuckerberg's decision-making and the two have a falling out. meanwhile, the winklevoss brothers sue zuckerberg for stealing their idea and claim that they are the rightful owners of thefacebook.\n\nthe movie is a gripping and engaging portrayal of the early days of facebook and the people who were involved in its creation. the dialogue is witty and fast-paced, and the acting is superb. jesse eisenb